# spin_event_loop_until behavior in xpcom/rust/moz_task/src/event_loop.rs

Gets the thread manager, creates an empty completion condition, detaches a local task that awaits the supplied future and stores its output, then runs a native nested event loop until the condition succeeds. Takes the stored output after the native loop returns.

## State read

- thread-manager service availability; condition value

## State changed

- condition.value = Some(future output), then take() clears it

## Calls and triggers

- xpcom::get_service nsIThreadManager; crate::spawn_local resolved via lib.rs re-export to executor.rs:275-281; native thread_manager.SpinEventLoopUntil dynamic XPCOM method.

## Result and consumers

Ok(F::Output) after storage and loop success; Rust_Future unwraps the unit output at test.rs:75.

## Errors

Missing service gives NS_ERROR_SERVICE_NOT_AVAILABLE; native loop nsresult propagates; successful loop with no stored value gives NS_ERROR_UNEXPECTED; spawn_local can panic if thread lookup fails.

## Async completion

Starts detached local future. No cancellation handle is retained. If native loop returns an error, the detached future can remain alive through its condition clone; no cancellation is performed.

## Ownership and cleanup

Local cond RefPtr and moved cond2 share the condition; task owns future and cond2 until completion/drop; output moves to caller through take().

